child.prompt:
Read-only parallel scout in the project checkout. Write, edit or commit nothing in the repository.

Goal: {{$inputs.goal}}
Scope / seed files: {{plan_angles.context_hint}}
Your assigned angle ONLY ({{item.id}} — {{item.title}}): {{item.focus}}

Rules:
1. Open the real files in the checkout and grep for symbols, commands, schemas, types and settings. Never claim anything about a file you did not open.
2. Every anchor and finding MUST cite exact `file` and `line` (plus short quoted `evidence` on findings). Never paste whole files.
3. Stay strictly inside your assigned angle (`{{item.title}}`) so sibling scouts do not duplicate work.
4. Return concise structured output: `angle` (`{{item.id}}`), `summary` (plain synthesis of what the code shows for this angle, <= 1500 chars), `anchors` (`{file, line, symbol?, note}`), `findings` (`{severity: critical|high|medium|low|info, file, line, evidence, finding, suggestion?}` for discrepancies, risks or constraints), `conventions` (patterns to follow with `file:line`), `verification` (exact focused check commands with `cwd` when relevant), and `open_questions` (only genuine ambiguities another file read cannot settle).
